# TG-04 stage B: the real tgd (TDLib, no account, no network) serving the window, on the
# volume tests/tg-install.script made. tgd --window asks for the api id and hash on its
# terminal (placeholders: api id 1 and a hash of zeros, which are no one's; the test DC);
# TDLib starts and waits for a phone number. Ended with Ctrl-C and started again in the
# background (the credentials kept), tgd serves tg, which connects and shows the login's
# phone form (the screen tgr-window). Nothing is sent to Telegram: the guest has no network.
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
type tgd --window --test-dc --no-probe\r
prefix tgd 0.1.0, TDLib
screen api id and hash from my.telegram.org (kept in the data directory)
prefix api id:
type 1\r
prefix api hash:
type 00000000000000000000000000000000\r
prefix OpenRouter key for the AI summary (Enter: none):
type \r
prefix tgd: the window's socket is /home/.config/tgd/window.sock
prefix tgd: login: starting
pause 3000
# Ctrl-C ends it (the credentials stay in its own directory); then tgd in the background,
# which asks for nothing now, and tg.
chord ctrl c
prefix tgd: login: closed
screen ~> _
chord ctrl l
top ~> _
type tgd --window --test-dc --no-probe &\r
prefix tgd: the window's socket is /home/.config/tgd/window.sock
pause 3000
shot tgr-tgd
type tg &\r
pause 6000
click 500 119
pause 1000
shot tgr-window
